Subject: [CANDIDATE] freedreno/a3xx: reject buffer resources as render targets

Buffer layouts do not have an image pitch. Advertising render-target
support lets reordered DISCARD_RANGE uploads choose a staging blit to
a buffer, then emit an invalid MRT pitch. Retain the existing buffer
copy/mapping path instead of sending an unsupported framebuffer to A3xx.

Device failure: 80-byte vertex buffer, pitch 1, bin_w 0, abort in
A3XX_RB_MRT_BUF_INFO_COLOR_BUF_PITCH. Requires device regression tests.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a3xx/fd3_screen.c
@@ -32,6 +32,13 @@
           util_format_name(format), target, sample_count, usage);
       return false;
    }
+
+   /* Buffer layouts have no image row pitch.  The A3xx render-target
+    * paths cannot use them, including the staging-upload blitter.
+    */
+   if (target == PIPE_BUFFER &&
+       (usage & (PIPE_BIND_RENDER_TARGET | PIPE_BIND_DEPTH_STENCIL)))
+      return false;
 
    if (MAX2(1, sample_count) != MAX2(1, storage_sample_count))
       return false;
